    <string name="wgk_tether_proxy_required">Set the proxy on the client. Without it the device has no internet at all — that is what guarantees nothing slips past the tunnel.</string>
    <string name="wgk_tether_howto">Android and iOS: Wi-Fi network settings → Proxy → Manual (or Auto with the config URL).\nWindows and macOS: system proxy settings, HTTP and HTTPS.\nBrowsers and terminals also accept the address as a SOCKS5 proxy.\nGames and Telegram usually ignore the system proxy — set the same address as a SOCKS5 proxy in the app\'s own settings, or they stay offline.</string>
    <string name="wgk_tether_error_tunnel_down">The tunnel went down, so sharing stopped.</string>
    <string name="wgk_tether_error_location">Turn on location in system settings: without it Android refuses to raise the access point, even with the permission granted.</string>
